WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.950
Introducing. The Shopping Agent on Your Side. For agents built anywhere.

2
00:00:02.000 --> 00:00:04.450
An outside agent wants to buy something. Lumen Assist, run by Lumen Labs, both fictional.

3
00:00:04.500 --> 00:00:06.950
Connect: Lumen Labs registers its agent. Identity says who answers for it; it authorises no spending.

4
00:00:07.000 --> 00:00:08.950
Discover: search and quotes are open; orders need a person's scope.

5
00:00:09.000 --> 00:00:11.450
Scope: Maya grants headphones, up to $200, three stores, until Thursday, in her own app.

6
00:00:11.500 --> 00:00:13.950
Request: signed request R-2207, headphones at $189 from homecircuit, for Maya.

7
00:00:14.000 --> 00:00:16.450
Evaluate: the rules layer checks identity, scope, limits, the signed offer and risk.

8
00:00:16.500 --> 00:00:19.450
Execute: the platform places the order with homecircuit; Northpay authorises $189 against her limits; Lumen gets the result, never card details.

9
00:00:19.500 --> 00:00:20.950
Record: one record for Maya, Lumen Labs, homecircuit and Northpay, from scope to delivery.

10
00:00:21.000 --> 00:00:23.950
Then Lumen asks to add a $39 warranty and ship to a new address. Refused: outside the scope, with a reason, and shown to Maya.

11
00:00:24.000 --> 00:00:25.950
Identity lets an agent in. Scope decides what it may do.

12
00:00:26.000 --> 00:00:27.450
Safe, Fast, Fun. Outside agents welcome. Inside the rules.

13
00:00:27.500 --> 00:00:29.950
The Shopping Agent on Your Side. Register technical interest.
